<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-10-14T20:15:25Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Nord Stream may have been lawful target, argue lawyers for Ukrainian accused of bombing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6dd12fee8309636001c0b6c393844c951aef24a3cacfbd5ee3f957685600a47f</id><updated>2026-10-14T20:15:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T19:56:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nord-stream-may-have-been-lawful-target-argue-lawyers-for-ukrainian-accused-of-bombing" /><summary type="html">Lawyers for a Ukrainian ex-military officer accused of leading the bombing of Russia's Nord Stream ​pipeline in September 2022 argued at the start of his trial in Germany on Wednesday that "an aggressor's infrastructure" may have been a lawful target. FRANCE 24's Juliette Brown reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Starlink restriction 'no surprise' after Musk condemned Ukraine strikes on Russian data centres</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e7d3311bebc627ebfd979e43f4fd48eef8347cf534e4c77cc8a1a11673db2092</id><updated>2026-10-14T20:15:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T19:49:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/starlink-restriction-no-surprise-after-musk-condemned-ukraine-strikes-on-russian-data-centres" /><summary type="html">Restrictions reported by Ukraine on its use of the US satellite internet system Starlink have exposed Kyiv's reliance on the technology for both offensive and defensive operations in its fight against Russia'a invasion, analysts and observers say. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Mark Owen, David Galbreath Professor of War and Technology at the University of Bath, says that "we always knew that allowing a private organisation like Starlink to have such a big impact on the combat operations in Ukraine was going to be challenging", explaining that "it is no surprise" that Starlink services had been throttled after SpaceX boss Elon Musk called the targeting by Ukrainian drones of data services in Russia "a step too far".</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump sparks outrage over AI tiger video after sharing footage of fatal UK attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c9cf116f3fb7c8ddf069f7c61538c590031974337056fd17bcaa51110c3a84ca</id><updated>2026-10-14T20:15:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T19:39:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/trump-sparks-outrage-over-ai-tiger-video-after-sharing-footage-of-fatal-uk-attack-1" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump has sparked outrage after sharing the distressing footage of a 23-year-old man with mental illness being fatally mauled by a tiger at Yorkshire Wildlife Park, captioned "Don't ever mess with nature!" This followed hours later by an AI-generated video of himself taming a tiger. The posts have been condemned as disrespectful to the victim, William Chapman, and his grieving family, who have urged people to stop sharing harrowing content of the attack. Vedika Bahl goes through it.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>How far will cockroach movement go? India's youth-led protests defy Modi government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cb56c417af0f1925f5e37cc336eb140d5ed948b2101984453e206e1627839db2</id><updated>2026-10-14T20:15:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T18:40:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261014-how-far-will-cockroach-movement-go-india-s-youth-led-protests-defy-modi-government" /><summary type="html">It all started as a bit of online satire by a few young people fed up by corruption. Clearly though, the Cockroach movement's no longer a laughing matter for India’s government which has shut transport and blocked rallying points in the capital to quell the momentum of youth-led mobilization that's already down the education minister over rampant school exam cheating and is now spearheading the protests against the culling of names from voter rolls, with the electoral commission chief accused of bias.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>‘Growing ambitions’: Dr. Kendall on Houthis’ quest to be recognised as Yemen’s ‘legitimate' leaders</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0e1cec7424a91a607dd6c6e560b031d4721e2240fc606d1db3551abd30e3c43c</id><updated>2026-10-14T20:15:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T17:18:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/growing-ambitions-dr-kendall-on-houthis-quest-to-be-recognised-as-yemen-s-legitimate-leaders" /><summary type="html">What is the strategic logic behind the Houthis’ increasingly high-risk confrontation with Saudi Arabia? “Their experience in the past is that threats pay,” explains Dr. Elizabeth Kendall, Middle East specialist and President of Girton College, University of Cambridge. Dr. Kendall argues that the movement’s increasingly audacious military operations are not merely expressions of ideological hostility or Iranian influence, but calculated instruments of political coercion aimed at securing legitimacy, expanding territorial control and strengthening its negotiating leverage.</summary></entry><entry><title>‘The idea that Modi must be feared because he holds all levers of power has gone out of the window’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ffaa44440d4747b044014a27a45abf6b1ce5228bd4c5d258cd8e7b1bf170537d</id><updated>2026-10-14T20:15:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T16:51:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/the-idea-that-modi-must-be-feared-because-he-holds-all-levers-of-power-has-gone-out-of-the-window" /><summary type="html">Is Narendra Modi losing his most powerful political asset: the perception of invincibility? As India's youth protest movement confronts an increasingly combative government, Dr. Subir Sinha, Director of the SOAS South Asia Institute and Reader in Development Studies, argues that the political significance of the demonstrations extends far beyond the arrests of opposition activists and the growing confrontation between protesters and state institutions. Dr. Sinha examines how the government's increasingly repressive response may be exposing the fragility of its authority and institutional legitimacy. Could India's emerging protest movement be dismantling the political mythology that has sustained Modi's hold on power?</summary></entry><entry><title>Houthis threaten escalation after strike on Saudi oil giant Aramco</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a36959e7d61122dac6117f35222c475214acccf2000fe736fb44f36300e05ca2</id><updated>2026-10-14T20:15:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T16:21:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261014-yemen-houthis-vow-continue-saudi-attacks-oil-giant-aramco-headquarters-hit" /><summary type="html">Yemen's Houthi rebels said Wednesday they had targeted facilities belonging to Saudi oil giant Aramco after officials in Riyadh reported a strike on a building in an area housing the energy giant's headquarters. The Iran-back militia also claimed missile strikes on the capital Riyadh and vowed to continue attacking Saudi airports and oil facilities.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>In Phoenix, young ultra-conservatives look to carry on Charlie Kirk’s legacy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8f9ed815a3beaacee3bfbf2c976879ad40fa752f0fe8c52a9d2ecc23d15db43e</id><updated>2026-10-14T20:15:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T14:37:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261014-in-phoenix-young-ultra-conservatives-look-to-carry-on-charlie-kirk-s-legacy" /><summary type="html">More than a year after the assassination of far-right influencer Charlie Kirk in September 2025, young activists from the organisation he co-founded, Turning Point USA, are working tirelessly to honour his legacy by rallying the youth vote ahead of the US midterm elections.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Houthis say targeted Saudi oil giant Aramco, vow more attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:99623e2e8c158ce53051f717e8c964d83cc3e59ad15bb6ae3626b3941633ae0e</id><updated>2026-10-14T20:15:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T14:00:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261014-houthis-say-targeted-saudi-oil-giant-aramco-vow-more-attacks" /><summary type="html">Yemen's Houthis said Wednesday they had targeted facilities belonging to Saudi Aramco, after Saudi officials reported a strike on a building in an area housing the energy giant's operations centre. Powerful explosions meanwhile rattled the Saudi capital, as the coalition fighting the Houthis said it had intercepted a missile fired by the Iran-backed group towards Riyadh.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ceuta an 'inalienable' part of Spain, king says on key visit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4b175242a2d7e02a386be3f81c8ec5f1aeb597339e11873ba0479b1630113e79</id><updated>2026-10-14T20:15:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T13:58:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261014-ceuta-an-inalienable-part-of-spain-king-says-on-key-visit" /><summary type="html">King Felipe VI on Tuesday said Ceuta and Melilla were "an inalienable part" of Spain as he made a landmark visit to the north African territories claimed by neighbouring Morocco. But the monarch, who rarely makes political interventions, emphasised Spain's need to "maintain good neighbourly relations" with Rabat after July's unprecedented migrant surge into Ceuta strained historically delicate ties. FRANCE 24's Sarah Morris reports from Madrid, Spain.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukraine accuses SpaceX of crippling military missions as ties with US worsen</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:715bb0669bdf54875d7e24ad135f7ed38396c79dae6d9325f213195f63e25195</id><updated>2026-10-14T20:15:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T13:57:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261014-ukraine-accuses-spacex-of-crippling-military-missions-as-ties-with-us-worsen" /><summary type="html">Ukraine accused Elon Musk's SpaceX on Wednesday of limiting Starlink services, crippling its drones, as Russian missiles knocked out power stations in attacks President Volodymyr Zelensky called "ostentatious disrespect" to Donald Trump. Kyiv's relationship with Washington has taken a sharp turn for the worse since US President Trump abruptly lifted sanctions on Russian diesel last week and publicly turned on Zelensky. FRANCE 24's Gulliver Cragg reports from Kyiv, Ukraine.</summary></entry><entry><title>Cornell University bans fraternity parties after alleged gang rape</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d9fb5030a660aa0f5449c07ad5a9924e38e80fdfda7015c2e3b3781272462ae3</id><updated>2026-10-14T20:15:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T13:55:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261014-cornell-university-bans-fraternity-parties-after-alleged-gang-rape" /><summary type="html">Cornell University will ban parties and social events at fraternity houses until the end of the academic year, its president said on Tuesday, responding to the outcry over an alleged ​gang rape on ‌campus in 2024. The measure is the strongest reaction yet from Cornell's leadership to a lawsuit ⁠filed by a former undergraduate, Jane Doe, alleging seven men sexually assaulted her during a party. Over the last several weeks, the Ivy League school in Ithaca, New York, and its ‌president, Michael Kotlikoff, have come under heavy criticism over its response to ⁠the allegations.</summary></entry><entry><title>School closures persist in France as protests gain momentum</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cf36bb275e11b59f8c30d99fc9fae5e7b9096e802962c734297cc4e387e3bd31</id><updated>2026-10-14T20:15:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T13:53:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261014-school-closures-persist-in-france-as-protests-gain-momentum" /><summary type="html">Some high schools in France remained closed on Wednesday, a day after tens of thousands of people joined rallies across the country to support protesting students. On Saturday, national demonstrations against the spiralling cost of living are to take place, and unions and student groups see the two protest currents fusing together.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukraine asking US, SpaceX and NATO to clarify Starlink limitations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bc1e2c9406501126490d8cee807d99005c876f8050468562916865ef83ec846e</id><updated>2026-10-14T20:15:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T13:52:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261014-ukraine-asking-us-spacex-and-nato-to-clarify-starlink-limitations" /><summary type="html">⁠Ukraine is ​in contact ​with the US, SpaceX and NATO to seek ​clarification ‌over ⁠limitations imposed on its access ‌to the Starlink satellite ⁠internet system, a source in the ​country's Defence Ministry ‌said on Wednesday. Ukrainian troops have reported that the Starlink ​connection is being shut off when travelling at ​higher speeds, causing major ​disruption to ​Ukrainian drone operations, many ​of which depend on satellite internet to pilot the craft. FRANCE 24’s International Affairs Editor Angela Diffley tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Yemen conflict escalates as Houthis say seized new strategic area</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:649fce44ae1d8990b2791032a4f48536e08d7f8caa5df042bcaa824e3a250911</id><updated>2026-10-14T20:15:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T13:50:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261014-escalating-conflict-in-yemen-as-houthis-say-seized-new-strategic-area" /><summary type="html">The Iran-backed Houthi rebels in Yemen released footage said to show operations in the Taiz governorate. Fighting between the Houthis and forces loyal to Yemen’s internationally recognised government, backed by Saudi-Arabia, has escalated dramatically in recent weeks after the Houthis managed to seize a number of strategically important areas, according to reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Duane Davis sentenced to minimum 40 years for Tupac killing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ac7c537a76e33c7959d06cbac17c6dd4aa39244016d7d729ac1c4fea0294887f</id><updated>2026-10-14T20:15:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T13:48:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261014-duane-davis-sentenced-to-minimum-40-years-for-tupac-killing" /><summary type="html">Duane Davis, the former Los Angeles gang leader who boasted in books and interviews of his involvement in the killing of rapper Tupac Shakur, only to deny it when he came to trial, was sentenced to a minimum 40 years in prison on Tuesday. FRANCE 24's Wassim Cornet reports from Los Angeles, United States.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Dark day for Turkey': Govt takes control of most-watched news channel</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:700f215f0eeca88c0a3e1a875b28b1c1d769d172a9ec3996c4dc7d334d193db2</id><updated>2026-10-14T20:15:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T13:47:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261014-dark-day-for-turkey-govt-takes-control-of-most-watched-news-channel" /><summary type="html">Police raided Turkey's most-watched news channel, Halk TV, early Wednesday, halting broadcasts and installing a government-appointed administrator in the latest move against pro-opposition media. Halk TV chairman Cafer Mahiroglu condemned the move against the broadcaster's Istanbul headquarters as "a dark day for Turkey", and criticism poured in from the opposition and rights groups.</summary></entry><entry><title>Guillaume Canet and Marion Cotillard reunite on the silver screen in thriller 'Karma'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:523b31021cfa5739c6cd45e904cbed16b271efa2bd82e222de5242bc487c79f5</id><updated>2026-10-14T20:15:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T13:34:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261014-guillaume-canet-and-marion-cotillard-reunite-on-the-silver-screen-in-thriller-karma" /><summary type="html">This week on arts24, our French film critic Manon Kerjean covers thrillers, history, legend and animation. "Karma" reunites exes Guillaume Canet and Marion Cotillard on screen for a thriller about a woman fleeing her past and the cult she escaped. "Moulin" follows Resistance hero Jean Moulin's final days in captivity, while "Le Fantôme de l'Opéra" returns for a modern retelling, but do critics buy it? We also discuss "Iron Boy", Louis Clichy's animated coming-of-age story inspired by his own childhood.</summary><category term="arts24" /></entry><entry><title>French MPs back bill to tackle sexual and gender-based violence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a649592da7f98dd1294ac9041aef5faefa20981fd458a6967e3de5e65f0096ad</id><updated>2026-10-14T20:15:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T12:58:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20261014-french-mps-back-bill-to-tackle-sexual-and-gender-based-violence" /><summary type="html">In France, a child is reportedly raped or sexually assaulted every three minutes. In a bid to put an end to sexual and gender-based violence, French MPs have voted for a comprehensive bill that could turn into law by the end of the year; it has yet to be debated by the more conservative Senate at the end of the month. FRANCE 24's Aurore Dupuis, who made the documentary "Broken children", tells us how this new law could help improve the situation for women and children in France.</summary><category term="Entre Nous" /></entry><entry><title>Cheap weapons, growing fears: Inside the Taliban’s drone campaign against Pakistan</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5e06ff93695892931958007142a88ae8088a7c38a9bdc0ba827a92aa3a407112</id><updated>2026-10-14T20:15:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T12:52:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261014-taliban-suicide-drone-attacks-pakistan" /><summary type="html">Pakistan says it intercepted 23 suicide drones launched from Afghanistan into Pakistani airspace in September alone. Since the conflict began in February 2026, the Taliban have increasingly used drones to attack Pakistan, raising concerns in Islamabad.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Louvre boss warns of closure risk unless museum is 'repaired, updated and transformed'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2d9c99731e57051986f440871b9574bc75bfb0a137ba707c1c798f29ac7d61ca</id><updated>2026-10-14T20:15:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T12:21:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/culture/20261014-louvre-boss-warns-of-closure-risk-unless-museum-is-repaired-updated-and-transformed" /><summary type="html">The world's most-visited museum "will eventually have to close its doors to the public" unless the French state steps in to finance a major overhaul, Louvre director Christophe Leribault told Le Figaro on Wednesday, in the latest dire warning about the creaking institution hit by a string of scandals including water leaks, ticket frauds and a high-profile jewel heist.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Trump's crackdown on migrants: New documentary investigates ICE operations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3a723778582e5e9781adc83b0c20cc3f7c836ee2beebf5ff212d0e2db80f3c1e</id><updated>2026-10-14T20:15:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T11:51:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261014-trump-s-crackdown-on-migrants-new-documentary-investigates-ice-operations" /><summary type="html">A new documentary from our sister channel France Télévisions explores US President Donald Trump's relentless crackdown on immigration and the agency carrying it out – United States Immigration and Customs Enforcement, better known as ICE. "ICE : La chasse a l'homme", or "A Manhunt Named ICE" interviews agents and also some of the people who lives have been turned upside down by ICE operations. In Perspective, we spoke to the film's co-writer Marine Pradel.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>French student protesters are being 'exploited' by political forces, Macron says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:118627b94e70986df9ee1da69593a47f1a74536fe6cace532b2cae22ec8b9892</id><updated>2026-10-14T20:15:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T11:33:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261014-macron-says-french-student-protesters-exploited-by-political-forces" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron said on Wednesday that France's student protesters are being "exploited" by political forces ahead of the country's presidential election in April 2027. Hard-left candidate Jean-Luc Melenchon participated in a Paris demonstration while hard-right frontrunner Marine Le Pen voiced support for the police deployed to protests.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Republicans weigh midterms strategy, pour money into campaigns even in red states</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0587f34162c0a344bf5e72c491646e4c9d6ee902e3ebbb24dfacb90124b718e1</id><updated>2026-10-14T20:15:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T10:56:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261014-republicans-weigh-midterms-strategy-pour-money-into-campaigns-even-in-red-states" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump said Tuesday Republicans face an equally difficult fight to retain control of the House of Representatives and the Senate in November's midterm elections, despite forecasts suggesting a considerably tougher contest in the House. Yet the party is pouring hundreds of millions of dollars into defending congressional and state-level seats once considered safely red. In some states, notably North Carolina and Georgia, they appear to be scaling back their ambitions – shifting resources to other Republican strongholds where Democrats are mounting unexpected challenges, as FRANCE 24's International Affairs Commentator Douglas Herbert explains.</summary></entry></feed>
